UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'Uses automated tools (where feasible) to regularly compare ICS/OT device configurations against approved baselines,
Provides alerts or reports when deviations are detected,
Implements compensating manual checks for devices lacking automation,
Schedules routine reviews (weekly, monthly, etc.) to ensure all discovered deviations are assessed and remediated promptly.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1453 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RECOMMENDATION'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'Do you have a central CM tool or a manual process for verifying OT device configuration compliance, and how often are settings checked?' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1453 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RISK'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'Without continuous or periodic validation of configuration settings, unauthorized changes or misconfigurations in ICS/OT devices can persist indefinitely. This increases the risk of exploitation by adversaries, system instability, or operational downtime caused by insecure or inconsistent configurations.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1453 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RISK-STATEMENT'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'CA-7' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1453 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-VULNERABILITY'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'The organization has not implemented or validated sufficient alternate controls to ensure operational continuity during disruptions (e.g. manual controls may not be regularly tested, redundant systems may lack proper configuration or maintenance, and alternative communication methods may not be established or functional). Current processes and resources are insufficient to maintain critical operations in the event of a cyber incident or other disruption.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1454 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-DISCOVERY'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'L' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1454 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-IMPACT'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'Establish and maintain alternate controls and processes to ensure operational continuity during disruptions to primary OT systems. This includes implementing redundant systems, manual fallback procedures, or other compensatory measures tailored to the organization''s operational needs. Regularly test and validate the readiness of these alternate controls through structured exercises, ensuring alignment with operational requirements and stakeholder expectations. Incorporate lessons learned from testing into updates to alternate control strategies, and ensure coordination with relevant internal and external stakeholders, including security teams and critical infrastructure partners.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1454 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RECOMMENDATION'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'How do you establish and maintain alternate OT control mechanisms, and how do you coordinate with security teams to ensure operational continuity during disruptions?' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1454 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RISK'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'The lack of operationally ready alternate controls and processes increases the risk of prolonged outages and operational disruptions during incidents affecting primary OT systems. Without alternate controls, the organization may face significant delays in restoring critical infrastructure services, which could impact public safety, economic stability, and national security. Untested or poorly coordinated alternate processes may fail to meet operational requirements, further exacerbating recovery efforts and undermining stakeholder confidence.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1454 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RISK-STATEMENT'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'CP-2, CP-6, CP-8, CP-9, CP-10, MA-6, PE-3, PE-11, PE-12, PE-17, SC-36, SI-13.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1454 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-VULNERABILITY'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'The organization has not effectively prepared OT personnel for specific incident response (IR) roles and has not integrated physical security measures or vendor coordination into its incident response processes. The lack of formalized planning leaves gaps in defining roles and responsibilities for internal operators, physical security teams, and external stakeholders during incidents. As a result, incident response processes for disruptions affecting OT systems remain undefined and unstructured, particularly when addressing both cyber and physical threats.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1455 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-DISCOVERY'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'L' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1455 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-IMPACT'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'The organization should establish a comprehensive incident response plan that encompasses both cyber and physical incidents, ensuring all relevant stakeholders are assigned clear roles and responsibilities. These roles should include internal OT personnel, physical security teams, and external vendors, where applicable. The plan must clearly document and communicate these responsibilities to ensure all parties understand their obligations during incidents involving unauthorized physical or cyber changes.
For physical security incidents, the plan should incorporate a physical validation checklist designed to verify the integrity of critical physical components, such as cabinets, network architecture, and other assets. This checklist should be utilized during and after incidents to confirm whether anything has been added, removed, or modified.
Regular training and exercises should be conducted to prepare all personnel involved in incident response activities, fostering effective coordination and readiness. The response plan should also be reviewed and updated periodically to account for lessons learned and evolving threats, ensuring the organization’s resilience against future incidents.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1455 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RECOMMENDATION'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'How do you assign and train OT staff for incident response roles, and integrate with physical security for effective handling?' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1455 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RISK'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'A lack of assigned and trained personnel for incident response introduces significant risks, including confusion and delays during both cyber and physical incidents. Without clear role definitions, internal staff may not be prepared to coordinate effectively with vendors, physical security teams, or other external stakeholders. This can result in miscommunication, mishandling of incidents, and prolonged recovery times. For physical incidents, such as intrusions or unauthorized access to facilities, the absence of integration with physical security teams can leave critical systems exposed to adversaries, compounding risks to safety and operational integrity.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1455 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RISK-STATEMENT'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'AC-2, CP-2, CP-4, IR-4, IR-7, IR-9, PE-6, PL-2, SA-15, SI-12, SR-8.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1455 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-VULNERABILITY'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'The organization does not have a formal reconstitution process for ICS/OT environments, lacks regularly tested backups or gold images, or does not verify integrity of restored systems. They may also lack procedures for using manual controls if the network must be taken offline for recovery.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1456 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-DISCOVERY'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'L' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1456 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-IMPACT'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'Develop and document a reconstitution plan specifically for ICS/OT, detailing how to rebuild or restore systems from trusted backups or gold images.
Regularly test backups and “gold images” in a non-production environment to ensure they can be restored quickly and safely.
Retain spare hardware (if feasible) to accelerate recovery when primary equipment is compromised or fails.
Validate system integrity (e.g., checksums, patches) before returning devices to production.
Train staff on using manual controls to maintain critical functions while reconstitution is in progress.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1456 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RECOMMENDATION'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'How do you ensure you can fully restore ICS/OT environments after an incident or disruption? Do you maintain tested backups, gold images, and spare hardware? Are there procedures for validating system integrity before returning to production, and do you have manual controls to sustain critical operations offline?' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1456 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RISK'
UPDATE [dbo].[MATURITY_QUESTION_PROPS] SET [PropertyValue]=N'Without a robust reconstitution process, the organization cannot reliably or quickly recover ICS/OT from a compromise or major disruption. Systems may remain vulnerable or unverified post-rebuild, increasing the risk of repeated compromise, extended downtime, or unsafe operations.' WHERE [Mat_Question_Id] = 1456 AND [PropertyName] = 'OBS-RISK-STATEMENT'
